;; expect: main.rawfn refused name_taken
;; the other direction of realize_name_taken: `rawfn` is a fn with no L meaning — a program and no
;; constant of K. A `def` under its name would give the name a second meaning: `h`, a typed fn
;; citing it, would be defined against the def (K proving h 2 = 5) while its program calls the fn (a
;; run printing 0). The def is refused
(import Init Nat.add)
(fn rawfn ((n Int)) Int (band n 1))
(def rawfn () (-> Nat Nat) (fun ((n Nat)) (Nat.add n 3)))
(fn h ((n Nat)) Nat (rawfn n))
